To create a dedicated page for each **coco** entry automatically, you can use HaruCMS’s page‑template system together with the **Pages** API.  
Here’s a quick, HaruCMS‑specific way to do it:

1. **Create a page template** (e.g., `coco-page.html`) that will be used for every entry.  
   ```html
   <!-- coco-page.html -->
   {for each entry in "coco"}
       {if entry.slug == "{page_slug}"}   <!-- page_slug will be replaced with the current page’s slug -->
           <h1>{ title }</h1>
           <div>{ description }</div>
           <!-- add any other fields you need -->
       {/if}
   {endfor}
   ```

2. **Add the HaruCMS client library** to the template so the `{}` syntax is rendered.  
   ```html
   <script src="/cms-template.v2.js"></script>
   ```

3. **Generate pages automatically** via the API.  
   Use the **Pages API** to create a page for every entry in the **coco** collection.  
   ```php
   // Example (run once, e.g., from a script or the admin panel)
   foreach ($entries as $entry) {
       $pageSlug = $entry['slug'];          // use the entry’s slug as the page slug
       $pageContent = file_get_contents('coco-page.html');
       // Replace {page_slug} placeholder with the actual slug
       $pageContent = str_replace('{page_slug}', $pageSlug, $pageContent);
       // Call the API to create the page
       $response = cmsClient.post('/api/pages.php', [
           'slug'    => $pageSlug,
           'content' => $pageContent
       ]);
   }
   ```

   The script above loops through every entry in the **coco** collection, creates a page whose slug matches the entry’s slug, and populates it with the template you defined.

4. **Result**  
   After running the script, you’ll have a dedicated page for each **coco** entry, all generated automatically—no manual page creation needed.
